From d3f401e4e503c4cca4a9782bf9202a3437c41735 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VLCKit Aloha Release <devnull@alohabrowser.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 12:55:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] apple/build.sh: compile all contribs with -fvisibility=hidden
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extend the flags passed to write_config_mak so every C-like compile flag
in contrib config.mak — CFLAGS, CXXFLAGS, OBJCFLAGS — carries
-fvisibility=hidden. With this in place, every contrib library (FFmpeg,
libvpx, libdsm, libplacebo, microdns, upnp, mpg123, …) ships its static
.a with all defined symbols marked `private external` (hidden Mach-O
visibility), so they cannot leak out of the final dylib that consumes
the VLCKit static archive.

This subsumes the FFmpeg-specific --extra-cflags=-fvisibility=hidden
already added in patch 0016 (contrib/ffmpeg: hide internal symbols on
Darwin) for FFmpeg, but is broader: it also closes the libvpx VP9
helper symbol leak (`_vp9_free_postproc_buffers`,
`_vp9_get_mvpred_av_var`) flagged by the 2026-05-15 spec's
done-definition nm check.
---
 extras/package/apple/build.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/extras/package/apple/build.sh b/extras/package/apple/build.sh
index 388c291096..f0ae5035e2 100755
--- a/extras/package/apple/build.sh
+++ b/extras/package/apple/build.sh
@@ -690,7 +690,7 @@ mkdir -p "$VLC_CONTRIB_INSTALL_DIR"
 
 # Write config.mak with flags for the build and compiler overrides
 # Set flag to error on partial availability
-write_config_mak "-Werror=partial-availability -U_LIBCPP_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS -D_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE=_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE_NONE"
+write_config_mak "-Werror=partial-availability -U_LIBCPP_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS -D_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE=_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE_NONE -fvisibility=hidden"
 
 # Write crossfile-meson with flags for the build and compiler overrides
 write_crossfile_meson
